---
source: misc/tests/help.rs
expression: "help_output(\"blkid\")"
---
Locate or print block device attributes (LABEL, UUID, PARTLABEL, PARTUUID, ID).

Resolution and listing go through the udev `/dev/disk/by-*` symlink layer. The on-disk
filesystem-signature probe path (`-p, --probe`) is **not implemented** in this v0 — invocations that
need it will exit with a clear error rather than silently returning incomplete data. Use upstream
`blkid` for probing.

Usage: blkid [OPTIONS] [DEVICES]...

Arguments:
  [DEVICES]...
          Devices to print attributes for; empty means list every device known to udev

Options:
  -L, --label <LABEL>
          Look up the device that uses this filesystem label

  -U, --uuid <UUID>
          Look up the device with this UUID

  -o, --output <FORMAT>
          Output format: `full` (default), `value`, `device`, `export`
          
          [default: full]

  -l, --list-one
          Only print the first match for -L / -U

  -d, --no-encoding
          Don't encode non-printing characters (no-op in v0; kept for command-line compatibility)

  -c, --cache-file <FILE>
          Cache file (ignored — v0 reads udev symlinks directly)

  -p, --probe
          Stub: probing isn't implemented in v0

  -i, --info
          Stub: probing-info isn't implemented in v0

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
